<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 84,688 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 84,688 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 84,688 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 33,376 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 6,931	    4,527</p>
<p>    Import cargo			77,757	   28,849</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    35,000	 Al-Sabiyah	   due</p>
<p>Gas oil		  27,000	 Nike		 24/11</p>
<p>Gas oil		  70,000	 Sea Islecity     22/11</p>
<p>Gas oil		  27,000	 Ras Al-Zour	23/11</p>
<p>Palm oil		  5,000	 Helena	     26/11</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Mirinda  26/11</p>
<p>high speed deisel    52,000	 Al-Maqwa	   28/11</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
